From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:02:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 127/131] compiler: dereferencing a loaded symtable again
 leaves what one dereference leaves

Re-resolving the symbol tables loaded from a ppu when a used unit is recompiled (a7b0e8a265)
dereferences them a second time. Three places assumed they run once:
- tgenericconstraintdata.deref appended the constraint interfaces to the existing list, so a
  constraint such as T: class, IFoo held duplicates and the old definition of IFoo;
- a copied enum, record or object def and an overriding indexed property took another counted
  reference to the shared symtable (getcopy) on every dereference and never gave the old one
  back (replace_copied_symtable keeps the reference for the same table, gives one for another
  table back, and leaves a table the def made for itself as it is);
- create_class_helper_for_procdef added a class helper method to its alias procsym again on
  every derefimpl.

Test: tests/tppu/reloadcopy (TTestRecompile.TestReloadCopy), a loaded unit with copied types, a
constrained generic and an overriding indexed property after control's new CRC recompiles base.
